scenario:
This is a two-player game between Player A and Player B. Every permanent below has been under its controller's control continuously since that player's most recent turn began, so none is summoning sick. All are untapped. No other permanents or effects are present.

Scenario 1 (attacking): It is Player A's turn, at the beginning of combat step. Player A controls two Ember Beasts (call them Beast 1 and Beast 2) and one Grizzly Bears. Player B controls no creatures. We consider which attack declarations Player A could legally make, with all attackers attacking Player B:
 (i) Beast 1 alone;
 (ii) Beast 1 together with Grizzly Bears, with Beast 2 not attacking;
 (iii) Beast 1 together with Beast 2, with Grizzly Bears not attacking.

Scenario 2 (blocking): This is a separate fresh game. It is Player A's turn. Player A controls a Hill Giant. Player B controls two Ember Beasts (Beast 1 and Beast 2) and no other creatures. Player A declares Hill Giant as an attacker, attacking Player B. In the declare blockers step, we consider which block declarations Player B could legally make:
 (iv) Beast 1 blocks Hill Giant, and Beast 2 does not block;
 (v) Beast 1 and Beast 2 both block Hill Giant.
